<ul>
  <li><strong>Handleless, precision-engineered design</strong> — the <a href="/brands/pronorm-german-kitchens">Y-Line and X-Line</a> seamless fronts are exactly the clean, warm contemporary look that Denver's Cherry Creek and the mountain-modern homes of Aspen and Vail specify.</li>
  <li><strong>Built for American kitchens</strong> — Pronorm offers 610mm (24″) cabinet depths as standard, unlike most German brands at 560–580mm, so no compromises on countertops, appliances, or storage.</li>
  <li><strong>Premium market position</strong> — fills the gap between entry-level German lines and ultra-premium names like SieMatic and Poggenpohl, opening a wide, under-served segment.</li>
  <li><strong>Protected territory &amp; strong margins</strong> — typical installations run $40,000–$150,000+ with design exclusivity in your market.</li>
